name: wasm_execute
version: "1.0.0"
language: zig
module: wasm_execute

description: |
  ACTUAL WASM INTEGRATION - Not design, but execution.
  This spec implements real WASM plugin loading with wasmtime,
  plugin API bridge, sandbox overhead measurement, and production
  validation of 3 example plugins.

types:
  WasmRuntime:
    fields:
      engine: WasmEngine
      linker: WasmLinker
      store_ptr: *mut c_void
      plugin_registry: Map<String, WasmPlugin>
      sandbox_overhead_ns: u64

  WasmPlugin:
    fields:
      name: String
      module_path: String
      instance: WasmInstance
      memory: WasmMemory
      guest_error: Option<GuestError>
      state: PluginState
      last_execution_ns: u64

  PluginState:
    enum:
      - Loaded
      - Initialized
      - Running
      - Failed
      - Unloaded

  GuestError:
    fields:
      code: u32
      message: String
      backtrace: List<String>

  SandboxConfig:
    fields:
      max_memory_pages: u32
      max_execution_time_ms: u64
      max_table_elements: u32
      enable_fuel: Bool
      fuel_per_call: u64

  PluginAPI:
    fields:
      host_print: HostFunction
      host_alloc: HostFunction
      host_free: HostFunction
      host_get_input: HostFunction
      host_set_output: HostFunction
      host_panic: HostFunction

  HostFunction:
    fields:
      name: String
      callback: FunctionPointer
      signature: String

  ExecutionResult:
    fields:
      success: Bool
      return_value: u64
      execution_time_ns: u64
      fuel_consumed: u64
      memory_peak_bytes: u64
      error: Option<String>

  BenchmarkMetrics:
    fields:
      native_time_ns: u64
      wasm_time_ns: u64
      overhead_ns: u64
      overhead_percent: f64
      iterations: u32

behaviors:
  - name: check_wasmtime_installation
    given: System environment
    when: Checking for wasmtime library availability
    then: |
      Returns installation status:
      - Check /usr/local/lib/libwasmtime.a
      - Check /usr/local/include/wasmtime.h
      - Try pkg-config --libs wasmtime
      - Return bool: true if available, false if missing
      - If false, provide installation command

  - name: create_wasm_runtime
    given: SandboxConfig with limits
    when: Initializing WASM runtime
    then: |
      Creates configured WasmRuntime:
      - Initialize wasmtime engine with config
      - Create linker with WASI support
      - Configure fuel metering if enabled
      - Set memory limits (max_memory_pages)
      - Set execution time limits
      - Return ready WasmRuntime or error

  - name: register_host_functions
    given: WasmRuntime with linker
    when: Registering Trinity host API
    then: |
      Adds all host functions to linker:
      - host_print: prints to stdout with plugin name prefix
      - host_alloc: allocate from plugin memory region
      - host_free: deallocate, validate pointer
      - host_get_input: retrieve input buffer pointer
      - host_set_output: set output buffer, validate size
      - host_panic: trap with error message
      - Return success or registration error

  - name: load_plugin_from_bytes
    given: WasmRuntime and WASM binary bytes
    when: Loading WASM module
    then: |
      Loads and validates plugin:
      - Validate WASM binary header (magic: 0x6d736100)
      - Compile module with engine
      - Instantiate via linker
      - Extract memory export
      - Extract guest_error export
      - Run _initialize() if present
      - Return WasmPlugin or LoadError

  - name: load_plugin_from_file
    given: WasmRuntime and file path
    when: Loading WASM plugin from disk
    then: |
      File-based plugin loading:
      - Read file to bytes
      - Validate .wasm extension
      - Call load_plugin_from_bytes
      - Store in plugin registry by name
      - Return WasmPlugin or FileNotFoundError

  - name: execute_plugin_function
    given: WasmPlugin and function name with input
    when: Calling plugin function
    then: |
      Executes plugin with sandboxing:
      - Set input buffer in host memory
      - Enable fuel metering if configured
      - Start high-resolution timer
      - Call plugin function via linker
      - Stop timer, calculate overhead
      - Read output buffer
      - Check guest_error for plugin panic
      - Return ExecutionResult with metrics

  - name: measure_sandbox_overhead
    given: WasmRuntime and plugin
    when: Benchmarking native vs WASM
    then: |
      Measures real sandbox cost:
      - Run native equivalent function 1000 iterations
      - Run WASM plugin 1000 iterations
      - Calculate: overhead = wasm_time - native_time
      - Calculate: overhead_percent = (overhead / native_time) * 100
      - Return BenchmarkMetrics with detailed breakdown
      - Include memory_peak_bytes tracking

  - name: compile_example_plugin_native
    given: Plugin source code
    when: Building native version for comparison
    then: |
      Creates native benchmark baseline:
      - Write C/Rust/Zig implementation
      - Compile with -O3 -march=native
      - Create shared library (.so/.dylib)
      - Return binary path or compilation error

  - name: compile_example_plugin_wasm
    given: Plugin source code
    when: Building WASM plugin
    then: |
      Compiles source to WASM:
      - Detect source language (C/Rust/Zig)
      - C: clang --target=wasm32-wasi -O3
      - Rust: cargo build --target wasm32-wasi --release
      - Zig: zig build-exe -target wasm32-wasi -O ReleaseFast
      - Optimize with wasm-opt (Binaryen)
      - Return .wasm path or compilation error

  - name: test_plugin_hello_world
    given: Loaded hello_world plugin
    when: Running hello_world example
    then: |
      Validates basic plugin:
      - Load plugin from output/hello_world.wasm
      - Call run() function
      - Verify output: "Hello from WASM!"
      - Verify guest_error is None
      - Return test result with overhead measurement

  - name: test_plugin_fibonacci
    given: Loaded fibonacci plugin
    when: Computing fib(20) in WASM
    then: |
      Validates computation plugin:
      - Load plugin from output/fibonacci.wasm
      - Call fib(20)
      - Verify result: 6765
      - Benchmark vs native Zig implementation
      - Return test result + overhead metrics
      - Expected overhead: <500ns per call

  - name: test_plugin_string_reverse
    given: Loaded string_reverse plugin
    when: Reversing "Trinity WASM"
    then: |
      Validates memory manipulation:
      - Load plugin from output/string_reverse.wasm
      - Call reverse("Trinity WASM")
      - Verify result: "MSAW ynirtT"
      - Verify memory cleanup (no leaks)
      - Return test result with memory usage stats

  - name: create_plugin_scaffolding
    given: Plugin name and language
    when: Generating plugin template
    then: |
      Creates ready-to-compile plugin:
      - Generate main.c/main.rs/main.zig
      - Include host API bindings
      - Provide example host_print() call
      - Provide Makefile with WASM target
      - Provide compilation instructions
      - Return project path

  - name: validate_plugin_sandbox
    given: Running WasmPlugin
    when: Checking sandbox isolation
    then: |
      Verifies sandbox guarantees:
      - Try to access host file system (should fail)
      - Try to access network (should fail)
      - Try infinite loop (fuel should stop it)
      - Try memory bomb (should hit limit)
      - Verify guest_error captures violation
      - Return list of blocked attempts
      - All must be blocked for validation pass

  - name: hot_reload_plugin
    given: WasmRuntime, plugin name, new WASM bytes
    when: Reloading running plugin
    then: |
      Zero-downtime plugin reload:
      - Load new module in parallel
      - Validate new module interface
      - Swap instance pointer atomically
      - Call cleanup on old instance
      - Update plugin registry
      - Return success or validation error

  - name: unload_plugin
    given: Loaded WasmPlugin
    when: Removing plugin from runtime
    then: |
      Clean plugin shutdown:
      - Call plugin's _cleanup() if present
      - Drop instance reference
      - Remove from registry
      - Return memory to pool
      - Verify no dangling references
      - Return success or cleanup error

  - name: get_plugin_metrics
    given: WasmPlugin
    when: Querying performance statistics
    then: |
      Returns detailed metrics:
      - Total execution count
      - Average execution time (ns)
      - Peak memory usage (bytes)
      - Total fuel consumed
      - Error count
      - Last error message
      - Return PluginMetrics struct

  - name: create_plugin_compatibility_test
    given: Two WasmRuntime instances
    when: Testing cross-instance compatibility
    then: |
      Validates plugin portability:
      - Load plugin in runtime A
      - Load plugin in runtime B
      - Execute same function in both
      - Verify identical results
      - Compare performance metrics
      - Return compatibility report
      - Must pass for production use

  - name: generate_wasm_bindings
    given: Plugin API specification
    when: Creating language bindings
    then: |
      Generates host API headers:
      - Generate wasm_plugin.h for C
      - Generate wasm_plugin.zig for Zig
      - Generate wasm_plugin.rs for Rust
      - Include function signatures
      - Include error codes
      - Include memory layout documentation
      - Return generated files paths

  - name: run_integration_suite
    given: All 3 example plugins compiled
    when: Executing full integration test
    then: |
      Production validation suite:
      1. Load all 3 plugins
      2. Run each plugin 100 iterations
      3. Verify outputs match expected
      4. Measure sandbox overhead (must be <1%)
      5. Verify memory cleanup (no leaks)
      6. Test hot reload on each plugin
      7. Test sandbox isolation on each
      8. Generate test report with metrics
      9. Return PASS/FAIL with detailed breakdown

  - name: create_production_example
    given: Real-world use case
    when: Demonstrating production deployment
    then: |
      Creates deployable plugin example:
      - Use case: Custom text transformation
      - Plugin: markdown_formatter.wasm
      - Host integration: Add to CLI pipeline
      - Configuration: Load from ~/.trinity/plugins/
      - Error handling: Graceful fallback
      - Documentation: README with plugin API
      - Return working example

  - name: setup_wasmtime_cmake
    given: Project without wasmtime
    when: Adding wasmtime dependency
    then: |
      Automates wasmtime integration:
      - Check if wasmtime installed (check_wasmtime_installation)
      - If missing, display install commands:
        * macOS: brew install wasmtime
        * Linux: curl https://wasmtime.dev/install.sh | sh
        * Build from source: git clone https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime
      - Add find_package(wasmtime) to CMakeLists.txt
      - Link wasmtime::wasmtime
      - Add include path for wasmtime.h
      - Return setup success with next steps

  - name: validate_wasm_binary
    given: Compiled .wasm file
    when: Checking binary validity
    then: |
      Validates WASM file:
      - Check magic number: 0x6d736100
      - Check version: 0x01
      - Validate module structure
      - Check required exports (memory, _initialize)
      - Check for forbidden imports (fd_write, clock_time_get if sandboxing)
      - Return validation report with issues
      - File is ready to load if valid

  - name: measure_memory_overhead
    given: WasmRuntime and plugin
    when: Calculating memory cost
    then: |
      Measures per-plugin memory usage:
      - Record baseline memory
      - Load plugin
      - Execute 10 iterations
      - Record peak memory
      - Unload plugin
      - Check for leaks (should return to baseline)
      - Return memory overhead in bytes
      - Expected: <1MB per plugin

  - name: create_plugin_dev_workflow
    given: Developer environment
    when: Setting up plugin development
    then: |
      Creates plugin development toolkit:
      - Generate plugin template (create_plugin_scaffolding)
      - Create Makefile with dev commands
      - Add watch script for auto-reload
      - Add test harness
      - Add documentation template
      - Return project structure with README
      - Developer can run 'make watch' for dev loop

example_plugins:
  - name: hello_world
    language: c
    source_path: examples/wasm/hello_world.c
    description: |
      Minimal plugin that prints "Hello from WASM!"
      Demonstrates host_print() usage and basic structure.
    compilation: |
      clang --target=wasm32-wasi \
        -O3 \
        -nostartfiles \
        -Wl,--export=run \
        -Wl,--export=_initialize \
        -Wl,--allow-undefined \
        -o hello_world.wasm \
        hello_world.c
    validation:
      function: run
      expected_output: "Hello from WASM!"
      max_overhead_ns: 100

  - name: fibonacci
    language: zig
    source_path: examples/wasm/fibonacci.zig
    description: |
      Compute Fibonacci number F(n) using iterative algorithm.
      Demonstrates performance benchmarking vs native code.
    compilation: |
      zig build-exe \
        -target wasm32-wasi \
        -O ReleaseFast \
        -fno-entry \
        --export fib \
        --export _initialize \
        -of fibonacci.wasm \
        fibonacci.zig
    validation:
      function: fib
      input: 20
      expected_output: 6765
      max_overhead_ns: 500
      benchmark_iterations: 1000

  - name: string_reverse
    language: rust
    source_path: examples/wasm/string_reverse.rs
    description: |
      Reverse string in-place using WASM memory manipulation.
      Demonstrates memory passing and buffer management.
    compilation: |
      cargo build \
        --target wasm32-wasi \
        --release \
        && wasm-opt \
        -O3 \
        -o string_reverse.wasm \
        target/wasm32-wasi/release/string_reverse.wasm
    validation:
      function: reverse
      input: "Trinity WASM"
      expected_output: "MSAW ynirtT"
      max_overhead_ns: 200
      check_memory_leaks: true

host_api_signature: |
  // C-compatible host API exposed to plugins
  #define HOST_API_VERSION 1

  // Print to host stdout (prefixed with plugin name)
  void host_print(const char* message, usize len);

  // Allocate memory in plugin's linear memory
  usize host_alloc(usize bytes);

  // Free previously allocated memory
  void host_free(usize ptr);

  // Get input buffer pointer and length
  void host_get_input(const char** buf_ptr, usize* len_ptr);

  // Set output buffer (copies to host memory)
  void host_set_output(const char* buf, usize len);

  // Trap with error message
  void host_panic(const char* message, usize len) __attribute__((noreturn));

  // Guest error structure (exported by plugin)
  typedef struct {
    u32 code;
    const char* message;
    usize message_len;
  } guest_error_t;

error_codes:
  - name: SUCCESS
    code: 0
    description: Operation completed successfully

  - name: ERROR_LOAD_FAILED
    code: 1
    description: Failed to load WASM module

  - name: ERROR_MISSING_EXPORT
    code: 2
    description: Required export not found

  - name: ERROR_MEMORY_LIMIT
    code: 3
    description: Exceeded memory limit

  - name: ERROR_FUEL_EXHAUSTED
    code: 4
    description: Computation exceeded fuel limit

  - name: ERROR_INVALID_POINTER
    code: 5
    description: Invalid memory access

  - name: ERROR_PANIC
    code: 6
    description: Plugin called host_panic

  - name: ERROR_SANDBOX_VIOLATION
    code: 7
    description: Attempted forbidden operation

  - name: ERROR_VERSION_MISMATCH
    code: 8
    description: Host API version mismatch

  - name: ERROR_UNKNOWN
    code: 255
    description: Unknown error

integration_tests:
  - name: test_plugin_lifecycle
    steps:
      - Load plugin
      - Verify state = Loaded
      - Run _initialize
      - Verify state = Initialized
      - Execute function
      - Verify state = Running
      - Unload plugin
      - Verify state = Unloaded
      - Verify no memory leaks

  - name: test_sandbox_isolation
    steps:
      - Load plugin
      - Try to read host file (should fail)
      - Try network access (should fail)
      - Try infinite loop (fuel stops it)
      - Verify all attempts blocked
      - Verify guest_error set

  - name: test_hot_reload
    steps:
      - Load plugin v1
      - Execute function
      - Load plugin v2 (different implementation)
      - Execute function
      - Verify new behavior
      - Verify old memory cleaned up

  - name: test_multiple_plugins
    steps:
      - Load 3 plugins simultaneously
      - Execute all concurrently
      - Verify no cross-plugin interference
      - Verify separate memory spaces
      - Unload all
      - Verify all memory returned

benchmarks:
  - name: hello_world_overhead
    description: Measure overhead of simple host_print call
    iterations: 10000
    max_overhead_ns: 50
    max_overhead_percent: 5.0

  - name: fibonacci_computation
    description: Compare native vs WASM for fib(20)
    iterations: 1000
    max_overhead_ns: 500
    max_overhead_percent: 1.0

  - name: string_reverse_memory
    description: Measure memory copy overhead
    iterations: 1000
    max_overhead_ns: 200
    max_overhead_percent: 2.0

  - name: plugin_load_time
    description: Time to load and initialize plugin
    iterations: 100
    max_load_time_ms: 10

  - name: memory_per_plugin
    description: Memory usage per loaded plugin
    max_bytes: 1048576  # 1MB

deliverables:
  - name: wasm_runtime.zig
    description: Core WASM runtime implementation
    path: src/wasm/runtime.zig

  - name: plugin_api.zig
    description: Host function bridge implementation
    path: src/wasm/plugin_api.zig

  - name: example_plugins
    description: Three working example plugins
    path: examples/wasm/
    files:
      - hello_world.c
      - fibonacci.zig
      - string_reverse.rs

  - name: integration_tests
    description: Full test suite
    path: src/wasm/test_integration.zig

  - name: benchmark_results
    description: Performance metrics
    path: trinity/output/wasm_benchmarks.json
    format: json

  - name: documentation
    description: Plugin development guide
    path: docs/wasm_plugin_guide.md

exit_criteria:
  - label: All example plugins compile successfully
    check: bash -c "ls -lh output/*.wasm | wc -l | grep -q 3"

  - label: All plugins load without errors
    check: zig build wasm-test

  - label: Sandbox overhead < 1%
    check: bash -c "jq '.overhead_percent < 1.0' trinity/output/wasm_benchmarks.json"

  - label: No memory leaks
    check: bash -c "jq '.memory_leaks == 0' trinity/output/wasm_benchmarks.json"

  - label: All integration tests pass
    check: zig build wasm-integration-test

  - label: Hot reload works
    check: zig build wasm-hot-reload-test

  - label: Documentation complete
    check: bash -c "test -f docs/wasm_plugin_guide.md && wc -l docs/wasm_plugin_guide.md | grep -q '[1-9][0-9][0-9]'"

next_steps:
  - name: Add plugin marketplace
    description: Share and discover community plugins
    priority: high

  - name: Add plugin signing
    description: Verify plugin authenticity and integrity
    priority: high

  - name: Add async plugin support
    description: Support async/await in plugins
    priority: medium

  - name: Add streaming data support
    description: Process large data in chunks
    priority: medium

  - name: Add plugin debugger
    description: Debug WASM plugins with breakpoints
    priority: low

tech_tree_branch: Runtime Architecture
dependencies:
  - wasmtime >= 15.0
  - zig 0.15.x
  - clang >= 14 (for C plugins)
  - cargo >= 1.75 (for Rust plugins)
  - wasm-opt (Binaryen, optional but recommended)

notes: |
  This spec is about ACTUAL EXECUTION, not design.

  Every behavior must include:
  - Real implementation (not "TODO")
  - Measurable success criteria
  - Error handling
  - Performance metrics

  The 3 example plugins MUST:
  - Compile successfully
  - Load in runtime
  - Execute correctly
  - Pass all tests
  - Demonstrate < 1% overhead

  If wasmtime is not available, setup_wasmtime_cmake will
  provide platform-specific installation commands.

  All behaviors are production-ready with real error handling,
  memory management, and performance measurement.
